0067: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0068:     """
0069:     Fire projectiles from 3-pixel triangle sprites; mark collisions with maroon or blue.
0070: 
0071:     Input structure:
0072:     - bg = most common color. Non-bg 3-pixel sprites shaped as axis-aligned L's or diagonal V's.
0073: 
0074:     Rule:
0075:     - Each triangle has an apex and an emission direction determined by its shape: L-shapes fire diagonally away from the missing corner; V-shapes fire along the axis away from the open side.
0076:     - A projectile lands exactly 5 cells from the apex in the emission direction.
0077:     - If it hits an existing sprite, that entire sprite is recolored to maroon (9).
0078:     - If two projectiles land on the same empty cell, that cell becomes blue (1); a lone projectile on empty bg paints maroon (9).
0079: 
0080:     Key insight: The triangle's orientation encodes both direction and target; dual-projectile collisions on open bg produce blue, not maroon.
